fn sec_cost io -> io
x12003 call open p0 13
x12004 write x12003 4
x12005 write x12004 1
x12006 text "cost"
x12007 puts x12005 x12006
x12008 call open x12007 11
x12009 write x12008 2
x12010 text "Cost"
x12011 puts x12009 x12010
x12012 call close x12011 
x12013 call open x12012 2
x12014 write x12013 4
x12015 write x12014 2
x12016 text "q"
x12017 puts x12015 x12016
x12018 write x12017 2
x12019 text "What does a whole edit cost a model, counting the instructions, the code it reads and its reply?"
x12020 puts x12018 x12019
x12021 call close x12020 
x12022 call open x12021 2
x12023 write x12022 4
x12024 write x12023 2
x12025 text "take"
x12026 puts x12024 x12025
x12027 write x12026 2
x12028 text "At 4000 functions an A0 edit costs 706 tokens against 143854 for TypeScript, which is 203.8x fewer than TypeScript shown the whole numbered file (A0's scoped view against a whole-file workflow, not both with scoped views). At 1 function A0 costs 2.42x TypeScript's tokens and 2.29x Rust's. Sonnet, cache-adjusted."
x12029 puts x12027 x12028
x12030 call close x12029 
x12031 call open x12030 2
x12032 write x12031 2
x12033 text "Cost here is every token a model reads and writes to make one edit: the instructions it is first given (the primer), the code it reads, and its reply. A model edits one function through a scoped view: the function, the signatures it depends on, and its callers. The view stays the same size as the program grows; a numbered whole file does not, so against a whole-file workflow A0's advantage grows with program size and reverses on a one-function file, where the primer dominates."
x12034 puts x12032 x12033
x12035 call close x12034 
x12036 call open x12035 2
x12037 write x12036 2
x12038 text "That is an advantage of the workflow, not of the language. When TypeScript, Rust, Python, Go, Java, C and Ruby are given an equal view (a parse-derived function and its callees, numbered line edits), pooled over the four program sizes (96 trials per cell) A0 canonical costs 318 tokens for one cold task and 176 in an unbounded session, against 386 and 138 for TypeScript and 375 and 115 for Ruby, so it is cheaper cold and dearer once the primer is cached; A0 dense costs 273 and 99. results/ai-edit-scoped.json."
x12039 puts x12037 x12038
x12040 call close x12039 
ret x12040
end

